WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.485
In this video, you will hide your contest from the public with two taps, and bring it back when you are ready.

00:00:06.485 --> 00:00:07.581
Nothing is deleted.

00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:08.677
We start on the map.

00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:13.640
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.765
That is the only address you need.

00:00:17.544 --> 00:00:19.951
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:19.951 --> 00:00:23.695
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:25.032
Tap Use my location.

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:31.217
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:34.422
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:38.982
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:45.184
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:45.184 --> 00:00:46.379
See the three dots?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.682
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:50.682 --> 00:00:51.220
Tap them.

00:00:52.824 --> 00:00:54.637
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:58.150
Tap Mine, your personal page.

00:00:59.849 --> 00:01:01.918
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:03.806 --> 00:01:07.978
On the Overview, the Controls card has a row called Contest page.

00:01:07.978 --> 00:01:09.938
It says Public and on the map.

00:01:09.938 --> 00:01:12.403
That means anyone can find the contest.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:17.587
Need to stop everything for a moment, for example to fix a mistake?

00:01:17.587 --> 00:01:18.469
Tap Unpublish.

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.780
It asks you to tap again, so it cannot happen by accident.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.226
Entries and votes stop, and the contest leaves the map.

00:01:27.226 --> 00:01:28.641
Tap again to unpublish.

00:01:30.621 --> 00:01:32.740
A red notice now sits at the top.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.853
It says the contest is hidden, and that nothing has been deleted.

00:01:36.853 --> 00:01:39.346
Your team can still open this dashboard.

00:01:40.247 --> 00:01:42.444
When you are ready, tap Publish it again.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:52.207
The notice is gone, the Contest page row says Public and on the map again, and entries and votes carry on, with everything still in place.

00:01:53.109 --> 00:01:58.133
That is Unpublish: hide the contest, fix what you need to, and publish it again.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.125
Nothing is lost.

00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:03.196
Next up: Add co-organizers and judges.
